"""Portable report for the applied whole-chain balance and its matched replays."""
import json,html
from pathlib import Path
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;run=HERE/'reports/investment-v2'
labels={'rush':'Minimal early factory','double':'Supported second line','triple':'Supported third line','overbuild':'Overinvest before upgrading','five-basic':'Five basic lines, then upgrade','small-late':'Keep the later factory small','large-late':'Expand the later factory further','weak-mining':'Only one Iron / Copper industrial miner','weak-structural':'Only one Structural Fabricator','weak-mechanical':'Only one Mechanical Assembler','weak-electrical':'Only one Electrical Assembler','weak-power':'Only one industrial generator','weak-fuel':'Keep basic coal supply','weak-fluid':'One Fluid factory — sufficient here','supported-basic-only':'Equivalent basic machinery + adequate power'}
rows=[]
for name,label in labels.items():
 r=json.loads((run/(name+'.replay.json')).read_text());e=[x['time'] for x in r['events'] if x['kind']=='reclaim' and x['detail'].startswith('smelter:')]
 rows.append(dict(id=name,label=label,minutes=r['seconds']/60,industrial=min(e)/60 if e else None,brown=r['brownoutSeconds']/60,energy=r['energyPUHours'],milestones=r['milestones'],success=r['success']))
base=next(x for x in rows if x['id']=='triple')['minutes']
early=rows[:3];body=''.join(f"<tr><td>{html.escape(x['label'])}</td><td>{x['industrial']:.1f} min</td><td><b>{x['minutes']:.1f} min</b></td><td>{x['minutes']-base:+.1f} min</td></tr>" for x in early)
chart=''.join(f'<div class="barrow"><span>{html.escape(x["label"])}</span><div class="bar"><i style="width:{x["minutes"]/180*100:.1f}%;background:{"#a9d88d" if x["id"] in ["triple","weak-fluid"] else "#e0b574"}"></i></div><b>{x["minutes"]:.1f}m</b></div>' for x in [rows[2]]+rows[5:])
page=r'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Factory · Investment balance v2</title><style>:root{color-scheme:dark}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#10171c;color:#edf2ee;font:15px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1320px;margin:auto;padding:32px}h1{font-size:36px;letter-spacing:-1px;margin:8px 0}h2{font-size:20px;margin-top:0}p{color:#a2b1b8}a,b{color:#a9d88d}.eyebrow{color:#a9d88d;letter-spacing:2px;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.metrics{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:18px;margin:25px 0}.metric,section{background:#1b252c;border:1px solid #354550;border-radius:12px;padding:22px}.metric strong{display:block;font-size:34px}.metric span{color:#a2b1b8;font-size:12px}section{margin-bottom:20px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px}th,td{padding:12px 7px;text-align:right;border-bottom:1px solid #354550}th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left}th{color:#a2b1b8;font-size:11px}.barrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:230px 1fr 65px;gap:12px;align-items:center;margin:13px 0;font-size:12px}.bar{height:9px;background:#30404a;border-radius:3px}.bar i{display:block;height:100%;border-radius:3px}.warn{color:#edbd6e}details{margin-top:18px}summary{cursor:pointer;color:#a9d88d}footer{color:#a2b1b8;font-size:12px;margin-top:20px}@media(max-width:800px){.grid{display:block}.metrics{grid-template-columns:1fr}main{padding:16px}.barrow{grid-template-columns:160px 1fr 50px}h1{font-size:28px}}
</style><main><div class="eyebrow">Economy lab / Applied investment-v2 balance</div><h1>Expansion earns its keep.</h1><p>Fund production, reach efficient machinery sooner, then expand the branches that actually constrain the Fighter.</p><div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><span>Supported third-line benchmark</span><strong>118 min</strong></div><div class="metric"><span>Earlier industrial operation vs minimal route</span><strong>18.2 min</strong></div><div class="metric"><span>Industrial mining / smelting power per item</span><strong>−50%</strong></div></div><div class="grid"><section><h2>Invest before industrial</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Early policy</th><th>Industrial smelter ready</th><th>Fighter</th><th>Vs third line</th></tr></thead><tbody>__EARLY__</tbody></table><p>These are complete packages with mining, workshops, fuel, generation and belts. The third line shares two basic Iron miners across the early material mix; adding a third Iron miner immediately was slower. Purchase order is part of the decision.</p><p>Four/five basic-line experiments approach parity or lose time. Their advantage has flattened before the jump to industrial. Full reclamation is retained, so excess construction is recoverable rather than a permanent resource trap.</p></section><section><h2>Power creates the upgrade incentive</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Equipment</th><th>Basic</th><th>Industrial</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Miner output</td><td>6/min</td><td>30/min</td></tr><tr><td>Miner power</td><td>14 PU</td><td>35 PU</td></tr><tr><td>Smelter output</td><td>6/min</td><td>30/min</td></tr><tr><td>Smelter power</td><td>24 PU</td><td>60 PU</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Five basic miners or smelters match one industrial machine's nominal throughput, but use twice its power. Their generators and coal supply are paid for too.</p><p>The reference late factory has 120 Iron/min of installed capacity: 20× the landing miner and 10× its doubled early Iron supply. Keeping one industrial Iron/Copper miner adds about 40 minutes.</p></section></div><section><h2>The bottleneck moves through the whole chain</h2><p>Each comparison changes the named part of the reference plan. Values are simulated completion times, not predictions of human skill levels.</p>__CHART__<p class="warn">One Fluid factory is enough at this milestone. Duplicating it does not pay back yet. Investment should follow demand, not a rule that every building must have three copies.</p></section><div class="grid"><section><h2>More useful production, less fixed waiting</h2><p>First research: <b>120 Plates + 40 Wire + 8 Refractory</b>. Later research demands more frames, motors, electrical parts and operating systems.</p><p>Frames now consume three Beams and three Plates. Drive units and cabinets consume more upstream components. Bay + Fighter material requirements expand to <b>1,787 Iron and 547 Copper ore</b>, before research, factory capital and fuel.</p><p>Fixed Bay/Fighter work falls from 52 to <b>20.8 minutes</b>; final research falls from 10 to 3 minutes. The saved time is used for meaningful production and investment decisions.</p></section><section><h2>Validation and limits</h2><p>All displayed routes finish. The reference route takes 117.875 minutes at 0.25-second ticks versus 118.25 at 0.5 seconds. Checked routes change by less than 30 seconds, preserving the conclusions.</p><p>Recovery, project and headless simulation checks pass. A fresh 12-policy search also finds a sub-two-hour route.</p><p class="warn">This is the applied Fighter-stage balance, not proof of a global optimum. Belt capacity and cost are modeled as pooled routes; physical layouts and player placement effort are not simulated. Existing executable builds require rebuilding.</p></section></div><p><a href="factory-planner.html">Explore factory capacity</a> · <a href="search-results.html">Latest batch search</a></p><footer>Applied catalog: investment-v2 · Reports, policies, source snapshots and timestep checks are saved under Tools/Balance/reports/investment-v2.</footer></main></html>'''
page=page.replace('__EARLY__',body).replace('__CHART__',chart)
(run/'comparison.json').write_text(json.dumps(rows,indent=2),encoding='utf-8');(run/'report.html').write_text(page.replace('href="factory-planner.html"','href="../../web/factory-planner.html"').replace('href="search-results.html"','href="../../web/search-results.html"'),encoding='utf-8');(HERE/'web/balance-v2.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
print(HERE/'web/balance-v2.html')
